":[{"id":"CHK-001","doc":"DOC-001","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Process Description","text":"Crude oil is pumped from tank T-101 by charge pump P-101A through suction valve XV-101 to the preheat train and heater F-101. A minimum flow line with FV-101 returns flow to suction on low flow. Seal flush follows API Plan 11 with quench."},{"id":"CHK-002","doc":"DOC-001","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Trip & Permissive Logic","text":"SEQ-101 start permissives: 1 Suction valve open (ZSO-101); 2 Seal flush established (dP > 1.5 bar) (PDI-101); 3 No active trip / reset done (DCS reset). Trips: PSLL-101 Suction pressure LOW-LOW < 0.3 barg; FSLL-101 Discharge flow LOW-LOW < 90 m3/h for 30 s; TSHH-101 Bearing temperature HIGH-HIGH > 95 degC; VSHH-101 Bearing vibration HIGH-HIGH > 9 mm/s."},{"id":"CHK-003","doc":"DOC-002","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Equipment Location Detail","text":"Crude Charge Pump P-101A: overall length 3200 mm, height 1100 mm, centreline elevation 450 mm, dry weight 4200 kg, motor 200 kW."},{"id":"CHK-004","doc":"DOC-003","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Plot Plan Layout & Legend","text":"Crude Charge Pump P-101A is at plot grid B-2, EL +0.00, footprint 5.0 x 3.5 m."},{"id":"CHK-005","doc":"DOC-004","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"OPL Header, Purpose & Hazard","text":"OPL-P-101A-01 Mechanical seal flush (API Plan 11) check (P-101A). Class: Trouble Case. Objective: Confirm seal flush dP above 1.5 bar before start. Fluid: Crude oil. Design 24 barg 120 degC."},{"id":"CHK-006","doc":"DOC-004","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Safety Precautions, Tools & Materials","text":"Safety: Apply LOTO and verify zero energy; Use gas detector in flammable service Tools: Torque wrench; Gas detector."},{"id":"CHK-007","doc":"DOC-004","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Procedure Steps","text":"Step 1. Line up flush to seal chamber (check: LOTO verified). Step 2. Check PDI-101 reads 1.5 to 2.5 bar (check: Within range). Step 3. Check no leak at seal (check: Dry)."},{"id":"CHK-008","doc":"DOC-004","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Common Problems & Troubleshooting","text":"Symptom: Crude leak at seal gland Cause: Flush orifice plugged Action: Cleaned orifice, replaced seal cartridge"},{"id":"CHK-009","doc":"DOC-004","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Key Learning Points & Sign-off","text":"Confirm seal flush dP above 1.5 bar before start."},{"id":"CHK-010","doc":"DOC-005","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"OPL Header, Purpose & Hazard","text":"OPL-P-101A-02 Pump start-up and priming (P-101A). Class: Basic Knowledge. Objective: Prime and vent the pump before every start. Fluid: Crude oil. Design 24 barg 120 degC."},{"id":"CHK-011","doc":"DOC-005","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Safety Precautions, Tools & Materials","text":"Safety: Apply LOTO and verify zero energy; Use gas detector in flammable service Tools: Torque wrench; Gas detector."},{"id":"CHK-012","doc":"DOC-005","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Procedure Steps","text":"Step 1. Open suction valve XV-101 (check: Valve open (ZSO-101)). Step 2. Vent casing at N5 (check: Liquid at vent). Step 3. Start motor and open discharge slowly (check: Flow above 90 m3/h)."},{"id":"CHK-013","doc":"DOC-005","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Common Problems & Troubleshooting","text":"Symptom: Pump does not build pressure Cause: Air in casing Action: Re-vent and re-prime"},{"id":"CHK-014","doc":"DOC-005","asset":"AST-001","page":1,"sec":"Key Learning Points & Sign-off","text":"Prime and vent the pump before every start."},{"id":"CHK-015","doc":"DOC-006","asset":"AST-004","page":1,"sec":"Process Description","text":"Product from the unit is received in tank T-201 and pumped to the terminal."},{"id":"CHK-016","doc":"DOC-007","asset":"AST-004","page":1,"sec":"Equipment Location Detail","text":"Product Tank T-201: overall length 12000 mm, height 10000 mm, centreline elevation n/a mm, dry weight n/a kg."},{"id":"CHK-017","doc":"DOC-008","asset":"AST-004","page":1,"sec":"Plot Plan Layout & 